---
import ComplianceShell from "../components/ComplianceShell.astro";
---

<ComplianceShell
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Agentura, including Agentura Test SMS Alerts."
>
  <p slot="intro" class="compliance-lead">
    This Privacy Policy explains how Agentura collects, uses, and protects information
    when people use our website, contact us, or opt in to Agentura Test SMS Alerts.
  </p>

  <section class="compliance-section">
    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      We collect information you provide directly, such as your name, email address,
      organization, message content, and any contact details you submit through our
      website or by email.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may also collect limited technical information, such as browser type, device
      information, pages visited, referring URL, and approximate usage data, to operate
      and improve the website.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="compliance-section">
    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>
      Agentura uses collected information to respond to inquiries, provide requested
      information, operate our website, maintain security, improve our services, and
      communicate about relevant account, service, or operational matters.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="compliance-section">
    <h2>SMS Messaging Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      If you opt in to receive SMS messages from Agentura, we collect your mobile phone
      number, consent status, consent timestamp, consent source, and SMS message history
      for the purpose of sending and managing Agentura Test SMS Alerts.
    </p>
    <p>
      SMS consent may be submitted through the Agentura SMS Opt-In page or by texting
      SUBSCRIBE to Agentura at (240) 221-6244.
    </p>
    <p>
      Agentura Test SMS Alerts are used for prototype account notices, scheduled
      maintenance reminders, and security/login alerts. Message frequency varies, up to
      10 messages/month. Message and data rates may apply.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell or share SMS opt-in data, mobile phone numbers, or SMS consent status
      with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may share SMS-related information with service providers that help us deliver
      and manage text messages, including messaging platforms, telecommunications
      carriers, and related vendors, solely as needed to provide the SMS messaging
      service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Users may opt out of SMS messages at any time by replying STOP. Users may request
      help by replying HELP.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="compliance-section">
    <h2>Service Providers</h2>
    <p>
      We may use trusted service providers to host our website, process communications,
      analyze site performance, support security, and deliver operational services. These
      providers are authorized to use information only as needed to provide services to
      Agentura.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="compliance-section">
    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide services,
      maintain records, comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our
      agreements.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="compliance-section">
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed
      to protect information. No internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed
      to be completely secure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="compliance-section">
    <h2>Your Choices</h2>
    <p>
      You may contact us to request access, correction, or deletion of personal
      information where applicable. SMS users may opt out at any time by replying STOP or
      request help by replying HELP.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="compliance-section">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, contact Agentura at
      <a href="mailto:hello@agentura.dev">hello@agentura.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</ComplianceShell>
